    ]
  },
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.habeas.fixme_graph` has no {test} references or :test: anchors. The requirement sets these obligations:\n- A FIXME acknowledgment is represented as a graph node.\n- Its tracking issues are exposed as labeled edges to GitHub issue nodes.\n- A named FIXME also connects to the requirement whose gap it acknowledges.\n- An unnamed FIXME connects directly to its tracking issues.\n- Every issue the acknowledgment names is available through its tracking edges.\n\nNone of these has a test, so the requirement has an adequacy gap. The scenarios that would be needed are a named FIXME, an unnamed FIXME, source ownership of the node, and an acknowledgment naming several issues.\n\nThe gap is acknowledged. `src/sdk.rs#enum[HabeasNode]` carries a `{fixme} requirements.sdk.habeas.fixme_graph` reference. Its body says: \"FIXME graph nodes and tracking-issue edges are deferred. Named/unnamed acknowledgments, source ownership, and multiple issue targets have no tests.\" That body describes the same missing tests. The reference names `nikomatsakis/habeas-codicem#26`, which is open.\n\nI searched `src/sdk.rs` for other FIXME-related tests. The only hits were `fn[outgoing_edges]` and `fn[populate_graph]`, which do not test the requirement, and an unrelated storage round-trip test with `fixmes:[]`.",
  "references": "1141b3c5566f1e6972b59af41cd4767fff054a9013c74f75d3919c488737eff3",
